test your pricing  if you want to have success as an  entrepreneur you want to make a lot of  money you've got to see what the right  price is for your market and you won't  know until you actually go  and test it most entrepreneurs  undervalue themselves under price  themselves and end up struggling to get  by  instead of being able to build a highly  successful company  hi i'm evan carmichael i believe that  hunger entrepreneurs deserve help  and today i'm answering a question from  a youtube viewer love you guys thank you  for writing in  intuitive heart healer intuitive heart  healer who wrote in to say hi evan i  found your videos i enjoy them thank you  my question to you  is this how do you go about finding  sponsors for youtube videos and more  importantly how do you figure out  what to charge them so for me  sponsorship on the youtube videos has  not been  one of the revenue streams that i'm  going after there are some ads that  might show up  um it's all run through youtube so  youtube finds  the partners it doesn't make a ton of  money i'm not making it rich off youtube  videos it's more to answer questions for  you guys  but if you are going to go out and find  a sponsor the typical way  that you would value it is based on a  number of views on your videos  so you could say i haven't checked your  channel so i don't know how many views  you have on your videos but for every  thousand views on your videos you're  gonna charge five bucks  eight bucks whatever makes sense and if  i were doing it i would also package in  an opportunity to be featured in the  video so if you are  showcasing their tools showcasing their  company  interviewing their president whatever  you can think of to do a video that's of  interest to your audience it's not just  a sales pitch  but helping them discover this great  company that you  passionately believe in then you could  charge more for it  so you might be able to charge a  sponsorship fee per video  and say it's five dollars per thousand  people who visit  and then you can also charge a  promotional piece where you are  showcasing  that company and sharing information  about them and why you think they're  great  and that could be a set fee maybe it's a  thousand dollars maybe it's 500  maybe it's 250 again whatever makes  sense you have to test  out your pricing start it  at a number that you feel is fair and  see what the reaction is  and then from there you can start  increasing your prices when i first  started doing  writing for big brands  i started off at 500 to do a piece  and people are really interested in that  it's like okay this is great i get 500  bucks  and i get the link to my own website  this is this is great this is bonus  i got too much demand i had i had too  many people coming to me who wanted to  do this and i didn't have enough time  to do it so i started increasing my  prices it was a thousand dollars  then it was fifteen hundred dollars and  now it's twenty five hundred dollars do  the same thing  and that seems to be the point for me  that seems to be the max  people people resist more on that price  so you can start off low you can start  off maybe a little bit under  what you think it should be at the end  and start  boosting yourself up as you get more  interest  see if it works it should the the  challenge for a lot of people who have  youtube channels is they don't get a lot  of views  so if you're basing on a thousand views  if you're making five bucks per thousand  views  which would still be a pretty good price  how many views are you getting on your  videos  right again i haven't checked out your  video so i don't want to assume that's  not a lot  but a lot of times the videos just are  not popular enough  so it might be really targeted which is  great but you have to have views to make  it count where you think you'll make  bigger money especially at the start is  if you do those promotional pieces  and you showcase why you like that  company good place to start but for any  entrepreneur  test your pricing at the start you're  just trying to get to survival  you're just trying to make enough money  to pay your bills so you don't have to  go back and get a job  okay but as you get better at what you  do as you become the expert you need to  start increasing your prices  and testing to see where your customers  start resisting because most  entrepreneurs could boost their prices  by 30 percent and if they're offering  incredible value  the customers won't care they won't  resist they'll keep paying  and you won't know that until you  actually go out and test it  so always be testing your prices and see  where you can bump it up because that  extra money goes right into your pocket  and i want you to have money in your  pocket thank you guys for watching you  like this video please give it a thumbs  up below and i want to hear what you  have to think  please leave a comment under this video  with your thoughts and if you have a  question let me know i want to hear from  you  i want to make a video reply for you  thank you so much and i'll see you on  the next episode

